# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repository shares: code, prompts, the JSON schema, the editable Dublin Core mapping,
# aggregate result tables, and chart images. What it does NOT share: the collection's data.
# Nothing under "data and catalog text" should be added until Special Collections confirms what can be public.
# (Comments must be on their own lines in a .gitignore.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- secrets (never commit a key) ----
.env
.env.*
*.key
*secret*
*credentials*

# ---- data and catalog text (hold until Special Collections confirms) ----
# catalog export: titles, notes, subjects
Prosch_Export.txt
# sample list with record titles
manifest.csv
# the photographs
images/
# AI output for each record, plus validation and score files
outputs/
# invalid model replies (they describe the images)
failed_runs/
# an older working copy
prosch_v2/
# vocabulary lists built from catalog subject headings, and cached id.loc.gov lookups for them
vocab_*.txt
vocab_classification.csv
id_cache.json
authority_cache.json
# shows images and catalog records side by side
review.html

# ---- derived files that contain AI text or catalog terms ----
review_*.xlsx
demo_review.xlsx
demo_dc_export*.csv
dc_export_*.csv
normalized_dates_*.csv
calibration_*.csv
confidence_v2_*.csv
unmatched_review*.csv
rubric_summary.csv
rubric_errors.csv
rubric_summary.md
logs_*.txt

# ---- working notes and findings that quote catalog headings (decide before publishing) ----
docs/
CLAUDE.md
CHECKLIST.md

# ---- Python and macOS clutter ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
